{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803145-are-there-any-mayan-incan-or-other-mesoamerican-bloodlines","id":803145,"title":"Are there any Mayan, Incan or other MesoAmerican Bloodlines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-07T09:11:37-08:00","id":803145,"title":"Are there any Mayan, Incan or other MesoAmerican Bloodlines?","content":"I'm creating a vampire based on Lady Six Sky the Mayan warrior queen, and I'm just looking for some Bloodlines from that region/time. Or even any based on the Spanish settlers/conquistadors that eventually arrived. Just anything that makes sense for around that period. I did a quick word search on WoD and nothing came up and I'm just not familiar enough with vampire to know where to look otherwise. I know that had vampire myths or at least, similar enough myths.<br /> <br /> Also, I realize she (late 600s) greatly predates most of the Covenants, (I didn't realize the Circle of the Crone was so young) so I'll probably just leave her unaligned - but if I'm wrong about that someone please let me know.<br /> <br /> Also, how would you guys translate the Mayan sciences to a character sheet? Science? Occult? Crafts? Academics? Would you bother at all? They had a lot of all of those things and were incredibly advanced for the period, but nowadays a lot of their advancements wouldn't really register on a normal person's character sheet. I mean, Calendars aren't exactly a big deal anymore. And their advancements in mathematics, astronomy and architecture are basically taken for granted as common place knowledge now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/c